# 👥 Customer Segmentation

The customer base consists of four major segments:

| Customer Segment | Customers |
| ---------------- | --------: |
| Mass Market      |     1,523 |
| Affluent         |       572 |
| High Net Worth   |       228 |
| Student          |       177 |

### Key Insight

**Mass Market** is the largest customer segment, representing the majority of the customer base.

---

# 💳 Transaction Analysis

The dataset contains **120,000 transactions** with an overall transaction value of approximately **₹355.30M**.

### Transaction Type

| Transaction Type | Approx. Total Value |
| ---------------- | ------------------: |
| Debit            |            ₹200.65M |
| Credit           |            ₹154.65M |

Debit transactions contribute a higher total transaction value than credit transactions.

### Transaction Categories

The analysis covers:

* Salary
* Transfer
* Shopping
* Loan Payment
* Utilities
* Travel
* Investment
* Dining
* Cash Withdrawal

### Key Findings

* **Salary** has the highest total transaction value.
* **Transfer** has the highest transaction volume.
* **Shopping** also represents a high transaction volume.
* Debit transactions have a higher overall value than credit transactions.

---

# 📱 Channel Analysis

The project analyzes five transaction channels:

* Mobile App
* POS
* Online
* ATM
* Branch

| Channel    | Transactions | Approx. Total Value |
| ---------- | -----------: | ------------------: |
| Mobile App |       38,570 |            ₹113.66M |
| POS        |       28,877 |             ₹86.62M |
| Online     |       28,558 |             ₹82.82M |
| ATM        |       14,317 |             ₹43.22M |
| Branch     |        9,678 |             ₹28.97M |

### Key Insight

**Mobile App** has the highest transaction count and highest total transaction value among the analyzed channels.

---

# 👤 Customer Activity Analysis

Customer-level activity was created using:

* Transaction Count
* Total Transaction Value
* Average Transaction Value
* Categories Used
* Channels Used

### Key Finding

**466 customers have no transactions** in the transaction dataset.

This group represents an opportunity for customer engagement and activation strategies.

---

# 📊 RFM Analysis

RFM analysis was used to understand customer behavior using:

### Recency

How recently the customer made a transaction.

### Frequency

How frequently the customer transacted.

### Monetary

How much transaction value the customer generated.

Customers were grouped into:

* 🏆 Champions
* 💎 High Value
* 🌱 Potential
* ⚠️ Low Value
* 💤 No Activity

RFM segmentation can help prioritize customer retention, engagement and cross-selling strategies.

---

# 📈 Power BI Dashboard

The Power BI dashboard contains **10 analytical pages**.

### 01 — Introduction

Project overview, objectives, tools and analytical scope.

### 02 — Executive Overview

High-level KPIs covering customers, transactions and transaction value.

### 03 — Customer Segmentation

Analysis of customer segments, customer distribution and demographic characteristics.

### 04 — Transaction Analysis

Transaction value, transaction volume, transaction type and category analysis.

### 05 — Channel Analysis

Comparison of Mobile App, POS, Online, ATM and Branch activity.

### 06 — Customer Activity

Identification of active, inactive and highly engaged customers.

### 07 — RFM Analysis

Customer segmentation based on Recency, Frequency and Monetary behavior.

### 08 — Time & Trend Analysis

Analysis of transaction activity across time.

### 09 — Customer Profile & Geography

Customer demographics and geographic distribution.

### 10 — Business Insights & Recommendations

Summary of major findings and recommended business actions.

